WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.834
Ali Vaez

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.869
is the director of the Iran Project

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.604
at the International Crisis Group,

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.240
and he's joining me now from Washington.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.510
Welcome back to the program.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.011
Thank you.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.345
Great to be with you, Christiane.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.513
So, okay, so look,

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.916
remind us where we were this time

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:17.884
five years ago

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.020
in terms of controlling

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.288
the Iranian nuclear program

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.358
and where we are now.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.994
So on eighth of May

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.965
20, 18, Iran was under the most rigorous

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.500
monitoring regime

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.802
that has ever been established by the UN

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.704
nuclear watchdog.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.006
It would take Iran about 12 months

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.641
to enrich enough

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.542
nuclear material

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.145
for a single nuclear weapon.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.547
And Iran was fully complying

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.216
by its obligations under the deal.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.752
And of course, by the time that President

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.922
Biden walked into the Oval Office,

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.924
that timeline had shrunk

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.692
and is now right now,

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.895
according to Pentagon officials,

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.329
at 12 days

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.465
instead of 12 months, it is 12 days.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.333
And Iran has rolled back

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.235
a lot of those monitoring mechanisms.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.671
And so the transparency of the program

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.038
is way

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.740
less than what it was in the past

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.041
than the IAEA is blind

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.043
about a lot of Iran's nuclear activities.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.579
So in one sentence, Christian,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:20.947
the Trump administration

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.816
managed to take Iran's nuclear program

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.184
out of a box

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.252
and to put it in the microwave.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.187
Wow.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.621
That's dramatic, the way you say that.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.824
So just just just be clear.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.358
The Trump administration said

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.960
that we can get a better deal

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.761
and they launched

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.696
a process called maximum pressure

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.331
where they tried to squeeze

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.500
Iran with more sanctions and a lot more

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.602
punitive measures,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.269
thinking that

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.471
that would cause them

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.473
to act in a different way.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:49.409
What exactly did maximum pressure achieve

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.012
Well, it has been an abject

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.481
failure across the board.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.081
Of course,

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.282
it has brought Iran

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.717
to the verge of nuclear weapons.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.853
Iran has never been closer

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.122
and it has also rendered

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.023
Iran much more aggressive

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.592
in the region in 2019.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.794
You remember the hot summer of that year

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.563
when Iran started attacking

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:14.167
shipping lanes and tankers and energy

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.335
infrastructure,

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.504
including in Saudi Arabia.

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.838
And it has rendered Iran

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.073
much more aggressive

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.941
and repressive at home.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.910
We have seen that every protest

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.546
that has happened since maximum pressure

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:29.382
has been met with the brutality

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.085
that we've all seen on on TV screens

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.920
in the past few years.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.422
And I will want to also add

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.091
that let's not

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.460
forget the fact that the Iranian people

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.128
have been living under

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:42.962
not just pressure

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:43.596
from the above,

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.597
from their own regime,

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.299
but also pressure from the outside,

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.935
from the United States and estimates

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.804
suggest that at least around

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:55.108
600 people have died as a result of short

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.110
shortages of medicine

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.511
that the US sanctions have caused

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.180
Oliver.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.782
So what then is the option?

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.650
We said,

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.618
and we know that there have been

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.587
basically indirect negotiations

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.321
between Iran

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.088
and the United States

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.089
via the Europeans

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.091
and the other signatories to the

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:12.625
what was known

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.228
as the JCPOA, the nuclear deal.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.163
But President Biden was caught

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.899
sort of off Mike not so long ago

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.268
saying that this deal is dead.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.104
Is it completely dead?

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.239
Is there any attempt?

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.942
I know that you and other experts

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:29.943
like Vali Nasr

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.711
and even J Street, the

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.346
the the Israeli activists,

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.582
the Jewish activist group in Washington,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:36.416
have called

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:40.420
for a different kind of engagement.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.590
Can you walk us through that?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.591
Sure.

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:45.592
First, Christian,

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.594
let me say that as a proponent

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.528
of the nuclear deal

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.262
with Iran, it's

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.464
very hard for me to admit that

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.433
the Biden administration

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.167
and the hardliners

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.401
in Iran succeeded

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.236
in what

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.537
President Trump failed at,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.439
which was to kill the JCPOA.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:00.607
Now, there's plenty of blame

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:01.941
to go around.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.110
I think obviously the original sin

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.647
was committed by Donald Trump But

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.283
but then the Biden administration

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:13.386
hesitated in 20, 21 and in 2022,

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.255
Iran miscalculated and lost

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.323
multiple opportunities

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.158
to restore the deal.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.627
Right now, as we speak,

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.528
I think the White House's preferences

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:25.365
for some kind of a narrower agreement,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.432
an interim deal

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.201
that would just freeze the program

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.336
so that it would not become a problem

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.504
in an election year

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:35.375
as we enter into the campaign period and

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.743
and the Iranians

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.411
are really not interested in

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:40.246
anything less than the JCPOA

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.181
because even the deal itself really

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.683
didn't benefit them economically

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.652
as much as the extent expected

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.920
a narrower deal would definitely

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.988
not do that.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.723
So we're currently in a situation

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.959
that I describe as no deal, no crises

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.294
that I think

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.261
the Biden administration

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.597
would want to extend until 20, 25.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.632
But there are two problems with it.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.334
Number one, it is unstable.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.635
We're really at the mercy

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:03.836
of a single incident.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.439
If Israel, for instance, commits

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.740
another sabotage

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.275
of an Iranian nuclear facility,

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:09.976
assassination

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.878
of an Iranian nuclear scientist,

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:12.578
we might see

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.180
significant escalation

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.650
in ways that would cross a US or Israeli

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.618
red line, for instance,

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:20.953
if the Iranians enrich to 90%.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.856
The second problem with with the strategy

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.392
is that imagine we can keep a lid on it

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.794
until 20, 25.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:28.728
Then what

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.829
in 2025

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.131
Iran would have 200% of the leverage

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.666
it had in 2015.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.435
It is not going to agree to a deal

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:36.135
that is tilted

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:38.037
more in the interest of the United States

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.372
is probably going to ask

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.140
for way more concessions

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.575
that even the next administration

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.544
would not be able to afford.

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:46.746
And that is why I think time has come

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.381
for a new thinking,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:50.149
different kind of thinking.

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.819
And what we are suggesting right now

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.988
is that if you look at

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.291
the current situation compared to 20, 15

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.693
and 2015, Iran had good relations

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.528
with the West and was on speaking terms

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.597
with the United States but bad relations.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.933
What its neighbors in the Gulf region

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.601
now is the other way around.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.670
And in that there is an opportunity

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:11.838
to make sure

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:13.339
that Iran can actually benefit

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.741
from an agreement

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:17.710
by encouraging the economic incentives

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.278
to go to Iran via

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:19.879
the Gulf

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.181
rather than from Europe

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.216
and the United States.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.450
And in return

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.619
Iran and the Gulf Cooperation

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.020
Council countries

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.222
could come to an agreement

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.456
that they would all

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.558
accept permanent limits

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:33.993
on the level of enrichment

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.261
and reprocessing

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.295
of plutonium

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.663
and on ratification

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.031
of the additional protocol,

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.566
which ensures

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.668
a very high level of transparency

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.070
in a permanent fashion.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:44.637
So let me

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.571
then put this to you,

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.806
because I've obviously interviewed

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.641
quite a few people on this,

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:49.942
because it is getting,

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:50.443
as you say,

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:53.513
to a very, very threshold level

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:55.681
and very rapid breakout level.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.850
I spoke to former Secretary of State

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.285
Hillary Clinton

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:01.020
not so long ago, but of course,

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.789
it was also at a time

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:04.023
which is still the case

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:05.558
where many people around

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:08.327
the world are very, very concerned

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:09.896
that what happened

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:10.963
in violating the human

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:12.632
rights of so many people in Iran

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:14.400
during the women's protests

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.301
the jailings,

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.569
the executions,

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.739
the sham trials, the crackdowns.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:22.475
None of this is conducive.

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.544
This is what Hillary Clinton told me

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:27.079
about the possibility of negotiating.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.583
I would not be negotiating

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.084
with Iran on anything

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:32.618
right now,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.353
including the nuclear agreement.

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.189
I think that, frankly, horse

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:37.123
is out of the barn

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:38.491
when Trump pulled us out.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.126
We lost

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.195
the eyes that we had

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:44.330
on what they were doing inside Iran.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.299
And I believe that

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:48.367
they started those centrifuges

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.469
spinning again.

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.604
And I think it's unlikely

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:54.474
that any agreement would be agreed to.

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:55.775
And I don't think we should look like

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:57.276
we're seeking an agreement

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:57.944
at a time

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:00.413
when the people of Iran are standing up

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.382
to their oppressors.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.685
So, I mean, that's a compelling case

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:08.287
for not dealing with them at this moment.

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.456
Do you think that still stands

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:13.593
is that kind of feeling and I understand

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.828
it exists in parts of the EU as well.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.131
Is that going to sort of

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.767
rule the day at the moment?

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:23.970
Look, the West can choose

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.404
not to negotiate with Iran,

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.973
but it wouldn't resolve the problem.

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.509
Iran's nuclear program is still advancing

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:30.610
at the speed of light.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.978
And at some stage

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.212
we would be once again

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.547
faced with the dilemma of

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:36.315
whether we can live with Iran

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:37.783
with a bomb or bomb Iran.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:38.551
And so

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:40.186
we would eventually get to that stage

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:42.021
unless we find a solution

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.055
And, you know,

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:43.656
it's true

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:44.957
that it's difficult

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:47.760
to deal with unsavory murderous regimes.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.663
But if we wanted to apply that logic,

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:51.631
for instance,

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:52.765
to the Soviet Union

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.800
and say that as long as the Soviet Union

00:08:55.101 --> 00:08:55.835
was engaged

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:57.069
in violations of human

00:08:57.069 --> 00:09:00.306
rights or policy or foreign policy,

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:01.374
that was problematic

00:09:01.374 --> 00:09:03.276
from the Western perspective,

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:04.944
we would never agree to arms control

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:06.212
deals with them.

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:07.079
We would be living in

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.881
a much more dangerous world right now.

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:11.350
And a regime like the Iranian regime

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:12.485
that cannot be trusted,

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:14.587
even with pellet guns, as we have seen

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:15.955
it has blinded

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:17.990
hundreds of peaceful protesters

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.292
in the past few months.

00:09:19.292 --> 00:09:21.594
How can we distrust this regime

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:23.663
with the deadliest weapons out there?

00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:25.898
And so I do believe that

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:28.167
regardless of the nature of the regime,

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.803
there is a need to find a solution to

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:31.871
this nuclear crisis.

